{
  "id": "Lyo.Authentication.Sso",
  "name": "Lyo.Authentication.Sso",
  "area": "Security",
  "tagline": "Protocol-neutral SSO host. Browser handoff, `/auth/*` endpoints, and the one-time user link plus JWT mint shared by OpenID Connect and SAML.",
  "description": "Protocol-neutral SSO host. OpenID Connect and SAML register an `ISsoProtocol` on `SsoProtocolRegistry`. This package owns the browser handoff, the `/auth/*` endpoints, and the user link plus JWT mint. It does not speak either protocol.",
  "features": [],
  "examples": [
    {
      "title": "Map the endpoints",
      "language": "csharp",
      "code": "using Lyo.Authentication.Sso.Endpoints;\n\nservices.AddLyoSso(builder.Configuration);\nservices.AddLyoOpenIdConnect();\napp.MapLyoAuthEndpoints();"
    },
    {
      "title": "LyoSso",
      "language": "json",
      "code": "{\n  \"LyoSso\": {\n    \"AllowedReturnOrigins\": [ \"https://app.example.com\" ],\n    \"DefaultReturnUrl\": \"/\",\n    \"HandoffCodeTtl\": \"00:00:30\"\n  },\n  \"LyoExternalLogin\": {\n    \"Policy\": \"JustInTime\",\n    \"RequireVerifiedEmail\": true\n  }\n}"
    }
  ],
  "sections": [
    {
      "type": "list",
      "title": "Endpoints",
      "items": [
        "`GET /auth/login/{provider}` starts the protocol registered for that name. A non-empty `returnUrl` that fails `IsAllowedReturnUrl` is 400 `InvalidRequest` before `StartAsync`. The error names `LyoSso:AllowedReturnOrigins`.",
        "`GET /auth/callback/{provider}` is the OpenID Connect path. The state cookie is `lyo_oidc_state` (HttpOnly, essential, SameSite=Lax, 15 minutes). It is set only when the protocol returns a sealed value.",
        "`POST /auth/callback/{provider}` is the SAML HTTP-POST path. It calls `DisableAntiforgery`. The form fields are `SAMLResponse` and `RelayState`. A GET to a SAML provider, or a POST to an OpenID Connect provider, is rejected before the body is read.",
        "`POST /auth/handoff/exchange` consumes the `lyo_handoff` code. `IssuedTo` is the origin of the return URL stored at login start, or the API origin when that URL is relative. The callback request origin is never `IssuedTo`.",
        "`mode=api` returns token JSON and writes no handoff code. That branch is for OpenID Connect. SAML completion always uses the browser handoff."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "title": "Options",
      "text": "`AddLyoSso(IConfiguration)` binds `LyoExternalLogin` and `LyoSso`. `AddLyoOpenIdConnect(IConfiguration)` does not bind these options itself."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "title": "Completion",
      "text": "`IExternalLoginCompletion` links the provider subject and mints one Lyo JWT. Provider scopes are stored on the link and are not copied onto the JWT. `JitFromAllowedClaim` matches a string or any entry of an `IReadOnlyList<string>`. A rejected login is 401, writes no handoff, and does not redirect to the return URL."
    }
  ],
